  5 Scroll prediction
    → (no translation)
  A lens over a feed is used while the feed scrolls. At the default rate the screen is captured every 125 ms, and the blocks that are placed from a frame captured at to are shown at a later display time t. If the content has moved by X (t) - X (to) points in between, an unpredicted block is that far from the text it translates. At a scroll speed of
    → (no translation)
