    → (no translation)
  old is v-0.125 = 125 points off, several lines of text. The
    → (no translation)
  reading and the translation of a frame take longer than that. Moving the finished blocks along with the page is therefore not an optimisation; without it the overlay is wrong whenever the page moves.
    → (no translation)
  5.1 Model
    → (no translation)
  The application cannot ask a page how far it has scrolled, and does not need to. It sees a scroll event anywhere on the screen (whether it scrolls what a lens reads is decided afterwards), and the system sends it with a time stamp, a signed delta d in the mits of the device, and a flag that says whether the deltas are precise (a trackpad: points, which browsers apply one to one) or fines (a mouse wheel: the application decides how many points a line is, and usually animates the step). Momentum scrolling needs nothing special: the system keeps sending events that decay.
